---
description: Routes must be REST resources only; non-REST needs a human-approved allowlist
alwaysApply: true
---

# REST routes only

Draw routes with `resources` / `resource` (optional `only:` / `except:` / `param:`). Actions are only the seven: index, show, new, create, edit, update, destroy. `root` may alias a REST show.

```ruby
# bad
get "reports" => "reports#weekly"
resources :invoices do
  post :pay, on: :member
end
```

```ruby
# good
resources :invoices, only: %i[index show]
resource :session
```

Do not use `get` / `post` / `put` / `patch` / `delete` / `match` / `mount`, or `member` / `collection` extras. If a non-REST route is required, stop and ask the human before drawing it. After they approve, list the path under Approved exceptions in this file.

Approved exceptions: none.
